    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers abandoned Llano del Medio around 1827–1828 after Apache and Comanche raids, resettling only in 1834.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/llano_del_medio_new_mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Genízaros, former captive Native Americans, moved east after 1786 peace treaties, bringing farming skills to Llano del Medio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/llano_del_medio_new_mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Llano del Medio sits at 5,239 feet (1,597 m) above sea level, giving it a high‑desert climate.",
